# Post-transaction notes shared by c0wrk-bin and c0wrk-git.
#
# Nothing here touches user data: the app creates ~/.c0wrk/config.yaml itself on
# first launch, and removing it on uninstall would destroy the user's provider
# credentials, sessions and database.

_c0wrk_notes() {
	cat <<'MSG'

c0wrk is installed to /opt/c0wrk (the binary, libonnxruntime.so and models/
must stay in one directory: the app resolves them relative to its own
executable). Launch it as `c0wrk-desktop` or `c0wrk`.

Configuration and data live in ~/.c0wrk/ and are created on first launch.

The built-in updater cannot install over a distro package: /opt/c0wrk is
root-owned, so it refuses the in-place swap and leaves the install untouched.
To stop being notified about updates that pacman will deliver anyway, add to
~/.c0wrk/config.yaml:

    updates:
      enabled: false

Optional runtime helpers: ripgrep (faster content search), git (project
features), wl-clipboard or xclip (clipboard integration).

MSG
}

post_install() {
	_c0wrk_notes
}

post_upgrade() {
	_c0wrk_notes
}
